    <string name="title_about_the_developer_section">About the developer</string>
    <string name="content_about_the_developer_section">I was a computer science student when I wrote the first lines of OpenWeather, and I have since become a developer. If I keep the app going in my spare time, it is because it has remained my playground: a project I carry from start to finish, at my own pace, where I try what I do not get the chance to try elsewhere.</string>
    <string name="title_about_your_data_section">About your data</string>
    <string name="content_about_your_data_section">No account, no tracking, no usage analytics. Your places and settings stay on this device. Only two things leave the phone: a place\'s coordinates, sent to OpenWeatherMap with your API key and language to get its weather, and the text you type in the search, sent to OpenStreetMap Nominatim.</string>
